.TH NP_PROCESSOR 3 "June 2026" "netpipe v0.1.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
np_processor_fn, np_processor_tcp_stream, np_processor_rate_limit, np_processor_payload_transform, np_processor_flow_tracker, np_processor_lua, np_pipeline_add_processor \- netpipe packet processors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <netpipe.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef np_err_t (*np_proc_fn)(np_packet_t *" pkt ", void *" userdata ");"
.PP
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_fn(np_proc_fn " fn ", void *" userdata ");"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_tcp_stream(void);"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_rate_limit(uint64_t " bytes_per_sec ");"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_payload_transform(const char *" mode ", const char *" pattern ", const char *" replacement ");"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_flow_tracker(void);"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_lua(const char *" script_path ");"
.br
.BI "np_err_t np_pipeline_add_processor(np_pipeline_t *" pl ", np_processor_t *" proc ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions create and attach packet processors or transforms to a pipeline.
Processors inspect, modify, rate-limit, or track packets as they flow through the pipeline.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_fn ()
function creates a custom callback-based processor.
Whenever a packet passes through this stage, the user-defined callback function
.I fn
is executed with a pointer to the packet and the user-supplied
.IR userdata .
The callback must return
.B NP_OK
to allow the packet to proceed, or a negative
.B np_err_t
to filter out the packet or indicate a pipeline error.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_tcp_stream ()
function creates a TCP stream reassembly processor.
It tracks TCP handshakes and sequence numbers to reconstruct application-layer payloads.
Reassembled payload bytes are attached to the packet structure as a contiguous stream, enabling deep packet inspection of application protocols (like HTTP and TLS).
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_rate_limit ()
function creates a Token Bucket rate limiter that throttles the pipeline's throughput to the specified
.I bytes_per_sec .
It delays packet delivery by calculating the elapsed high-resolution CPU time and sleeping the pipeline worker thread when the bucket is empty.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_payload_transform ()
function creates a payload replacer/transformer.
It searches for a specific byte or string
.I pattern
in the packet payload and replaces it with
.I replacement .
The parameter
.I mode
can define regex or literal substitution modes.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_flow_tracker ()
function creates a flow tracking processor.
It maps packets to bi-directional conversations (flows) based on the five-tuple (source/destination IP, source/destination port, protocol) and assigns unique flow IDs.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_lua ()
function loads and executes an external Lua script specified by
.I script_path
for every packet.
This allows writing dynamic packet manipulation or analysis logic in Lua.
.PP
The
.BR np_pipeline_add_processor ()
function attaches a processor to the pipeline.
Processors are executed sequentially in the order they are added.
Processors added to a pipeline are owned by the pipeline and automatically freed when
.BR np_pipeline_free ()
is called.
.SH RETURN VALUES
Processor creation functions return a pointer to a newly allocated
.B np_processor_t
on success, or
.B NULL
on failure.
.PP
.BR np_pipeline_add_processor ()
returns
.B NP_OK
on success, or a negative
.B np_err_t
code on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libnetpipe (3),
.BR np_pipeline (3),
.BR np_packet (3)
